@startuml service-planner
title **Planner** — a service, and the one process it runs\nnamed graphs are shown by TYPE, never by name

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam titleFontSize 15
skinparam ArrowFontSize 11
skinparam database {
  BackgroundColor #E8F1F8
  BorderColor #5B8DB8
}
skinparam folder {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #8FB4D0
  FontSize 11
}
skinparam component {
  BackgroundColor #EAF5EA
  BorderColor #5E9E5E
}

component "**Planner**\n<i>service</i>\n\nruns **Planning**\n<i>process</i>\n\nbounded search over\nsimulated worlds" as PL #D6EBD6

database "Beliefs\n<i>repository</i>" as BEL {
  folder "ag:ActionGraph\nthe templates" as t1
  folder "ag:WorldGraph" as t2
  folder "ag:StateGraph" as t3
  folder "ag:PickRecordGraph" as t4
  folder "ag:ObligationsGraph" as t5
  folder "ag:DeliberationGraph\nthe trace" as t6 #F2FBF2
}

database "Desires\n<i>repository</i>" as DES {
  folder "no graph class\nretired by #312" as d1 #FDF2F2
}

database "Imaginarium\n<i>repository</i>" as IMG {
  folder "ag:PossibleGraph\none per search node" as p1 #F2FBF2
}

t1 ..> PL : templates to walk
t2 ..> PL
t3 ..> PL
t4 ..> PL
t5 ..> PL
d1 ..> PL : the wants
p1 ..> PL : the world reached so far

PL --> p1 : **writes** — reached()
PL --> t6 : **writes** — candidates, verdict

note right of PL
  **Returns, never stores:** a `Plan` of steps.
  Only the head is committed, by **execution** —
  a different service. The tail is trace.
end note

note bottom of IMG
  **One service, one output MODALITY.**
  `ag:DeliberationGraph` is a subclass of
  `ag:PossibleGraph`, so both writes are
  possible-modality: the worlds that die with
  the pass, and the trace that survives it
  because the health series read it.
  ----
  Provenance forces *every graph has ONE
  author* — a function from graph to service,
  not a bijection. `inference` writes two graph
  types, `sensing` two, `review` three. A graph
  carries author AND subject.
  ----
  **The Desires repo cannot be drawn by type.**
  Its two graphs have no class (#312), so the
  one rule this diagram follows — name the
  CLASS, never the instance — has nothing to
  name. Every other repository can.
end note
@enduml
